                      <X>3287.3813</X>
                      <Y>65</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cc" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>3287.3813</X>
                      <Y>135.54102</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cd" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>3038.462</X>
                      <Y>135.54102</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A quick note</item>
                    <item name="Font" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Arial</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">75028de7-18a3-44dd-89c1-6632fdca1aaf</item>
                    <item name="Italic" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 1  -  Set back the slab edge
Goal: each floor outline pulled in slightly from the facade.
Idea: Scale about each floor's own centre point shrinks it
   evenly: 0.98 = 2% smaller.
Watch for: Scaling about the world origin would also slide the
   slab sideways: use each floor's centre.
Wire check: setback slider -&gt; F (factor), centre points -&gt; C.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
