                    </item>
                    <item name="Cd" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>3472.462</X>
                      <Y>114.84277</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A quick note</item>
                    <item name="Font" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Arial</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">b8bdd7c0-0e7d-40ec-bfa6-8b29d26f9ba5</item>
                    <item name="Italic" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 2  -  Slab thickness, downward
Goal: the slab thickness as a negative number.
Idea: Multiplying by -1 flips the direction: each slab hangs
   below its floor line instead of sitting on top.
Watch for: The -1 is typed into the B input; it isn't a slider.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>3467.462</X>
                          <Y>60</Y>
                          <W>244.37354</W>
                          <H>59.842773</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                          <X>3472.462</X>
                          <Y>65</Y>
                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
            <chunk name="Object" index="61">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7f5c6c55-f846-4a08-9c9a-cfdc285cc6fe</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="13">
                    <item name="Bold" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Ca" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>3895.462</X>
                      <Y>65</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cb" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4143.384</X>
                      <Y>65</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cc" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4143.384</X>
                      <Y>114.84277</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cd" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>3895.462</X>
                      <Y>114.84277</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A quick note</item>
                    <item name="Font" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Arial</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">a319edf0-89dd-4cb8-9566-9d24f7ecbe5a</item>
                    <item name="Italic" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 3  -  Point it down
Goal: a vector as long as the slab is thick, pointing down.
Idea: The same Unit Z as Level B: a negative factor makes it
   point down.
Watch for: Unit X and Unit Y would push the slabs sideways.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>3890.462</X>
                          <Y>60</Y>
                          <W>257.92188</W>
                          <H>59.842773</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                          <X>3895.462</X>
                          <Y>65</Y>
                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
            <chunk name="Object" index="62">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7f5c6c55-f846-4a08-9c9a-cfdc285cc6fe</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="13">
                    <item name="Bold" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Ca" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4223.384</X>
                      <Y>65</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cb" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4473.1953</X>
                      <Y>65</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cc" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4473.1953</X>
                      <Y>125.191895</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Cd" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                      <X>4223.384</X>
                      <Y>125.191895</Y>
                    </item>
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A quick note</item>
                    <item name="Font" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Arial</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">37e6b4a3-94e3-4000-8ec2-12405a6ed49d</item>
                    <item name="Italic" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Scribble</item>
                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 4  -  Give floors thickness
Goal: each floor outline pushed down into a slab.
Idea: Extrude pushes a curve along a vector. A closed outline
   becomes the edge of a slab.
Watch for: The direction is a vector, not a number.
Wire check: outlines -&gt; B (base), vector -&gt; D (direction).</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="1">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="2">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>4218.384</X>
                          <Y>60</Y>
                          <W>259.81152</W>
                          <H>70.191895</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31">
                          <X>4223.384</X>
                          <Y>65</Y>
                        </item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                  </chunks>
                </chunk>
              </chunks>
            </chunk>
            <chunk name="Object" index="63">
              <items count="2">
